  "derivation": [
    "parse_rule preserves a valid outer rule and inner diagnostics; no wrapper bytes in atrule input.",
    "The adopted policy rejects all six singleton character-variant definitions, preserving their empty subsidiary block and the outer rule. All six styleset definitions survive in source order.",
    "Descriptor validation emits at declaration start; with_descriptor_context maps to InvalidDescriptorValue; inferred encountered token is the original identifier at that position.",
    "RuleBodyParser consumes through semicolon for the first five failures. Final open-6 has no semicolon, so its recovery span ends immediately before the block closing brace at byte 100.",
    "Structural recovery uses DropDescriptor; report ordering sorts by responsible source byte. Input is ASCII on one line, so UTF-8 byte offsets equal UTF-16 columns.",
    "No outer rejection, implicit closure, resource-limit, or additional diagnostic is warranted by this complete bounded input."
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "Fonts4 6.9.1 versus 6.9.2 remains normatively unresolved for character-variant cardinality, character-variant first range, and styleset range.",
    "Only cardinality conflict affects this original input; its positive small styleset values satisfy both sections.",
    "Expectations were independently predicted under documented policy; runtime equality has intentionally not been evaluated."
  ],
  "scope": "Original singleton character-variant corpus input under the adopted provisional implementation policy. Normative conflicts remain unresolved.",
  "policy_provenance": "Recovered describes the CSS-owned expected implementation behavior under documented Fonts4 section 6.9.1 policy, not a standards-conflict resolution. L02-R104 through L02-R106 remain unresolved-standard. The earlier at-rule-reconciliation.json unresolved singleton is retained as historical uncertainty.",
